## An Animated Desktop Media Player for Wayland

Many desktop music widgets are bloated, rely on heavy web technologies, or lack
personality. **CapyPlayer** is a lightweight, native desktop widget built in
Rust and Slint that brings interactive, customizable music players directly to
your Linux desktop surface.

Whether playing music through Spotify, Firefox, or a local media player,
CapyPlayer syncs live with your media sessions to display playback states,
spinning vinyl record animations, and real-time audio spectrums.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Key Pillars & Features

### 1. The `capy-mpris` Engine

Under the hood, CapyPlayer is powered by **`capy-mpris`**, a standalone,
high-performance Rust crate built on `zbus`. It manages Linux media sessions
with:

* **Efficient Resource Management:** Uses a single persistent D-Bus connection
  instead of repeatedly spawning processes.
* **Smooth Playback Interpolation:** Calculates song progress smoothly on the
  client side without continuously burdening media players with status requests.
* **Smart Player Prioritization:** Automatically switches to the active source
  when you alternate between Spotify and a browser tab, for example.
* **Reusable Library:** Designed as a decoupled crate that can also be used in
  taskbars, status bars, or CLI tools.

### 2. Modular, Animated Vinyl Skins

CapyPlayer includes multiple visual themes for any desktop layout:

* **Realistic Turntable:** A nostalgic record player with a spinning vinyl disk
  and playback controls.
* **Compact Turntable:** A sleek, vertical design ideal for sidebars or smaller
  screens.
* **Vinyl Card:** A modern horizontal card with track information, album art,
  and an integrated audio visualizer.

### 3. Dynamic Color Extraction & Adaptive Styling

The widget automatically analyzes the dominant colors of the current album
artwork. The background glow, accent colors, and interface elements dynamically
adapt their color palette with every new song.

### 4. Native Wayland & Desktop Integration

* **Layer-Shell Support:** Integrates seamlessly as a desktop layer within
  modern Wayland compositors (such as Hyprland, Niri, Sway, and River).
* **Smooth CAVA Visualizer:** Displays real-time frequency bars and audio
  animations directly on the card.

### 5. Hot-Reloading Configuration

Switch skins or adjust settings directly in `~/.config/capy-player/config.toml`
— changes take effect immediately without needing to restart the application.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Technologies Used

* **UI Toolkit:** Slint UI (compiled native GUI).
* **Programming Language:** Rust.
* **Media & D-Bus:** `capy-mpris` (custom standalone crate based on `zbus`).
* **Desktop Protocol:** Wayland Layer-Shell (via `spell-framework`).
* **Audio Visualization:** CAVA audio spectrum processor.

## Skins

### Realistic Vinyl Player

A skeuomorphic turntable layout. It includes a singular button to play/pause the
current track &.

<AssetImage name="realistic-vinyl-player.gif" alt="Realistic Vinyl Player" />

### Compact Vinyl Player

A streamlined, vertically oriented deck designed for compact screen real estate
or sidebar placement. It includes play/pause, next & previous buttons.

<AssetImage name="compact-vinyl-player.gif" alt="Compact Vinyl Player" />


### Vinyl Card

A sleek horizontal card showcasing track metadata, vinyl album art and an audio
visualizer. Clicking on the vinyl will hide the rest of the card, only
displaying the vinyl.

<AssetImage name="vinyl-card.gif" alt="Vinyl Card" />

